+      <section class="about-hero"><p class="eyebrow">About ONYX Athletic Club</p><h1 class="about-hero-title">Strength is a<br /><em>lifelong practice.</em></h1><p class="about-hero-desc">Since 2018, ONYX has been the room where people come to get stronger — and stay for who they become. Coaching-first, community-built, and honest about the work it takes.</p></section>
+
+      <section class="about-stats" aria-label="ONYX in numbers"><div><strong>8</strong><p>years of<br />showing up</p></div><div><strong>12K<span>+</span></strong><p>members<br />and counting</p></div><div><strong>40<span>+</span></strong><p>expert coaches<br />in your corner</p></div><div><strong>150<span>+</span></strong><p>sessions<br />every week</p></div></section>
+
+      <section class="about-story section-pad"><div><p class="eyebrow">Our philosophy</p><h2>Train with<br /><em>purpose.</em></h2></div><div class="about-story-copy"><p>ONYX started with a simple observation: most gyms sell access. Rows of machines, a swipe card, and good luck. We think people deserve more than access — they deserve direction.</p><p>Every session at ONYX is coached, every program is progressive, and every member is known by name. We measure success not in check-ins, but in first pull-ups, first 5Ks, and the quiet confidence of people who trust their bodies again.</p><p>That is what “harder to break” really means to us — not just stronger muscles, but sturdier lives.</p></div></section>
+
+      <section class="about-values section-pad"><p class="eyebrow">What we stand for</p><h2>Principles that<br /><em>never rest.</em></h2><div class="about-value-grid"><div class="about-value"><span>01</span><h3>Coaching first</h3><p>Every session is led, not left to chance. You will never have to guess what to do next.</p></div><div class="about-value"><span>02</span><h3>Consistency over intensity</h3><p>We program for years, not weeks. Progress you can keep beats progress you can post.</p></div><div class="about-value"><span>03</span><h3>Community as equipment</h3><p>The room raises your bar. Training alongside people who show up makes you someone who shows up.</p></div><div class="about-value"><span>04</span><h3>Recovery is training</h3><p>Rest is where the work lands. Mobility and recovery are programmed in, never bolted on.</p></div></div></section>
+
